  {
    "id": "0befbd1bf96f43c3cfdb22bf",
    "path": "deltalake_core::datafile::reader::ParquetTableReader",
    "name": "ParquetTableReader",
    "owner": null,
    "crate": "deltalake-core",
    "version": "1.0.0+58f07cd6",
    "kind": "struct",
    "signature": "struct ParquetTableReader",
    "docs": "Dataset-tier reader that reads all of a table's parquet data files directly —\nno DataFusion, no predicate — composing [`ParquetFileReader`] across the table.\n\nMinimal by design: it reads raw parquet, so [`ParquetTableReader::try_new`]\nrejects tables that use deletion vectors, column mapping, or partition columns\n(those are the kernel-backed [`KernelDataReader`]'s job), and it does not unify\nschemas across files — returned batches reflect each file's physical schema as\nwritten. On a table whose schema evolved, older and newer files yield batches\nwith differing schemas, and the caller must reconcile them (e.g. cast to a\ncommon schema before `concat`).",
